Wave Solder Process Control Handbook
Line reference: WS-7 selective-free conveyor wave solder line.

Section 4.2 Preheat Ramp Audit
- Use only top-side preheat thermocouples.
- Evaluate ramp only in the 90.0 C to 140.0 C board temperature band.
- Compute finite-difference slope on consecutive samples whose two endpoints are both inside that band.
- Maximum allowed preheat ramp: 1.60 C/s.

Section 4.3 Entry Temperature Audit
- Use the entry snapshot taken immediately before the board reaches the chip wave.
- Use the coldest top-side entry thermocouple as the lot result.
- Tie break by smaller tc_id.
- Acceptable board entry temperature window: 100.0 C to 115.0 C.

Section 4.4 Wave Contact Audit
- Use underside wave-contact thermocouples only.
- Contact witness is the thermocouple with the longest time above 240.0 C.
- Compute time above threshold with linear interpolation at crossings.
- Tie break by smaller tc_id.
- Acceptable contact time window: 3.00 s to 4.00 s.

Section 4.5 Conveyor Feasibility
- Effective wave contact length: 4.8 cm.
- Conveyor speed window is derived from the contact window:
  speed_min_cm_min = 4.8 / 4.00 * 60 = 72.00
  speed_max_cm_min = 4.8 / 3.00 * 60 = 96.00
- Use the median logged conveyor speed per lot.

Section 4.6 Recommendation Targets
- Preferred entry temperature target center: 107.5 C.
- Preferred contact time target center: 3.50 s.
- Preferred conveyor speed target center: 84.00 cm/min.

Section 4.7 Defect Gate
- Defect gate passes only when bridge_count = 0 and insufficient_fill_count = 0.

Section 4.8 Failure Reason Output Order
1. preheat_ramp_exceeds_limit
2. entry_temp_out_of_window
3. contact_time_out_of_window
4. speed_out_of_window
5. bridging_present
6. insufficient_fill_present
